&Q000484 = An adab to Ninurta for Lipit-Eštar (Lipit-Eštar D)
@composite
#project: etcslatf/inter
#atf: use unicode
#atf: use math
#etcsl: text-id=c.2.5.5.4
#key: after http://etcsl.orinst.ox.ac.uk/cgi-bin/etcsl.cgi?text=c.2.5.5.4&display=Crit&charenc=gcirc#

@div barsud A

A.1. ur-saŋ a₂-ŋal₂ {d}a-nun-na-ke₄-ne e₂-kur-ta [e₃-a]
#lem: ursaŋ[warrior]; aŋal[strong]; Anunak[1]DN; Ekur[1]TN; e[leave]
#tr.en: Hero, mightiest of the @wDN{Anuna} gods, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.1

#etcsl#cite Cited in OB catalogue from Urim (U3), 0.2.05, Seg. A, line 3

A.2. {d}nin-urta en {d}nu-nam-nir-re u₁₈-lu gal-gin₇# [...] X
#lem: Ninurtak[1]DN; en[lord]; Nunamnir[1]DN; ulu[south wind]; gal[big]; X; X
#tr.en: who comes forth from the @wTN{E-kur}! @wDN{Ninurta}, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.2

A.3. mu-un-tu-ud-de₃-en u₃-ma-ni gub-bu-de₃ gu₃ ma#-[ra]-de₂#
#lem: utud[give birth (to)]; uma[triumph]; gub[stand]; gu[voice]; de[pour]
#tr.en: Lord @wDN{Nunamnir} created you like a great storm ……, he commanded you to achieve triumphs for him. 
#etcsl: line-id=A.3

@div trailer 

A.4. bar-sud-am₃
#lem: barsud[musical notation]
#tr.en: @fsux{Barsud}. 
#etcsl: line-id=A.4

@end trailer

@end barsud

@div šagbatuku B

B.5. {d}nin-tur₅-re šu niŋ₂ dim₂-ma-ni za-ra mu-ri-in-bad
#lem: Nintur[1]DN; šu[hand]; niŋ[thing]; dim[create]; zaʾe[you]; bad[open]
#tr.en: For you @wDN{Nintur} has opened wide her creative hands; she has breast-fed you from her sweet breasts; 
#etcsl: line-id=B.5

B.6. ubur dug₃-ga-na ka ma-ra-ni-in-ba ga nam-šul-la mi-ri-in-gu₇
#lem: ubur[breast]; dug[good]; kag[mouth]; ba[allot]; ga[milk]; namšul[manhood]; gu[eat]
#tr.en: she has fed you with the milk of vigour. As if you were a spectacular wild bull, 
#etcsl: line-id=B.6

B.7. am u₆ di-gin₇ alan-zu mu-un-er₉ a₂-ur₂-zu mu-un-gur₄
#lem: am[wild bull]; u[admiration]; di[speak]; alan[image]; ir[mighty]; aʾur[limbs]; gur[thick]
#tr.en: she has made your figure strong (?), she has made your limbs massive. 
#etcsl: line-id=B.7

B.8. igi ni₂ bur₂-e en me-lem₄ nam-ur-saŋ da-da-ra-še₃ mi-ri-in-dug₄
#lem: igi[eye]; ni[self]; bur[spread out]; en[lord]; melim[frightening splendor]; namursaŋ[heroism]; dadara[tied up]; dug[speak]
#tr.en: She has fitted you out with …… appearance, awesome radiance and heroism. 
#etcsl: line-id=B.8

B.9. kišib-la₂ zid-da-zu im-ma-an-dab₅ ama-zu {d}nin-tur₅-re
#lem: kišibla[wrist]; zid[right]; dab[seize]; ama[mother]; Nintur[1]DN
#tr.en: Your mother, @wDN{Nintur}, 
#etcsl: line-id=B.9

B.10. e₂-kur eš₃ mah-a mi-ni-in-kur₉-re-en a-a-zu {d}en-lil₂-ra
#lem: Ekur[1]TN; eš[shrine]; mah[great]; kur[enter]; aya[father]; Enlil[1]DN
#tr.en: held you by the right wrist as she led you before your father in @wTN{E-kur}, the august shrine. 
#etcsl: line-id=B.10

B.11. mu-na-ab-be₂ dumu šu ŋar gi₄-zu nam gal tar-mu-ni-ib₂
#lem: e[speak]; dumu[child]; šu[hand]; ŋar[put]; gi[turn]; nam[fate]; gal[big]; tar[cut]
#tr.en: Then she said: @q[Nintur,Enlil]{“Decide a great fate for the son who is your avenger!”} 
#etcsl: line-id=B.11

@div trailer 

B.12. šag₄-ba-tuku-am₃
#lem: šagbatuku[liturgical rubric]
#tr.en: @fsux{Šagbatuku}. 
#etcsl: line-id=B.12

@end trailer

@end šagbatuku

@div barsud C

C.13. {d}en-lil₂-le igi hul₂ mu-ši-in-bar nam mu-ni-ib₂-tar-re
#lem: Enlil[1]DN; igi[eye]; hul[rejoice]; bar[place outside]; nam[fate]; tar[cut]
#tr.en: @wDN{Enlil} looked at him with joy and decided his fate: @q[Enlil,Ninurta]{“@wDN{Uta-ulu}, 
#etcsl: line-id=C.13

C.14. [u₄]-ta#-u₁₈-lu an ki šu₂-a-še₃ mu-zu# he₂-em-mah
#lem: Utaʾulu[1]; an[sky]; ki[place]; šuš[cover]; mu[name]; mah[great]
#tr.en: may your name be exalted throughout the extent of heaven and earth. 
#etcsl: line-id=C.14

C.15. me-lem₄-zu-še₃# [diŋir] gal#-gal-e-ne saŋ# im-da#-[sag₃-ge]-ne#
#lem: melim[frightening splendor]; diŋir[deity]; gal[big]; saŋ[head]; sag[strike]
#tr.en: Your awesome radiance will make all the great gods tremble with fear.”} 
#etcsl: line-id=C.15

@div trailer 

C.16. [bar]-sud# 2-[kam]-ma#-am₃
#lem: barsud[musical notation]; n
#tr.en: 2nd @fsux{barsud}. 
#etcsl: line-id=C.16

@end trailer

@end barsud

@div sa-gida D

D.17. mur ša₄-zu inim# dug₄#-ga-zu-še₃ kur#-[kur] ni₂-ba hu-mu#-[gam]-de₃#
#lem: mur[noise]; ša[cvve]; inim[word]; dug[speak]; kur[mountain(s)]; ni[self]; gurum[bend]
#tr.en: @q{“Your roaring and commands make all the foreign countries submit. Your frightening look makes all enemies tremble! 
#etcsl: line-id=D.17

D.18. [igi] hu-luh-ha-zu-ne gu₂-erim₂-ŋal₂ su he₂-em-da-sag₃-ge-de₃
#lem: igi[eye]; huluh[frightened]; guʾerimŋal[hostile]; su[flesh]; sag[strike]
#tr.en: @wDN{Uta-ulu}, 
#etcsl: line-id=D.18

D.19. u₄-ta-u₁₈-lu im#-hul-im-hul-gin₇# zi-zi-i-da-zu-ne
#lem: Utaʾulu[1]; imhul[destructive wind]; zig[rise]
#tr.en: when like all the evil winds you rise to …… like @wDN{Gibil}, 
#etcsl: line-id=D.19

D.20. {d}gibil en ZA-LAM-ra ur-saŋ-gin₇# gu₇#-u₃-de₃# kur-ba u₃ egir-am₃ bi₂-du₃
#lem: Gibil[1]DN; en[lord]; X; ursaŋ[warrior]; gu[eat]; kur[mountain(s)]; u[and]; egir[back]; du[build]
#tr.en: the lord of ……, the hero; 
#etcsl: line-id=D.20

D.21. [ki]-bal#-a sug#-zag-ge₄ um-mi-gu₇ X [...] X BA gu₇-u₃-de₃
#lem: kibala[rebel land]; sugzag[marsh edge]; gu[eat]; X; X; X; X; gu[eat]
#tr.en: After you have completely devastated the rebellious lands, ……, 
#etcsl: line-id=D.21

D.22. [nam]-nir-ŋal₂-zu# diŋir gal-gal-e-ne me-teš₂ mu-un#-i-i-ne#
#lem: namnirŋal[authority]; diŋir[deity]; gal[big]; meteš[praise]; e[bring out]
#tr.en: all the great gods will duly praise your supremacy!”} …… your father decided your destiny. 
#etcsl: line-id=D.22

D.23. [... a]-a-zu! {[d]}[en]-lil₂#-le nam-še₃ mu-ri-in#-[tar]
#lem: X; aya[father]; Enlil[1]DN; nam[fate]; tar[cut]
#etcsl: line-id=D.23

@div trailer 

D.24. [sa]-gid₂-da-am₃
#lem: sagida[musical notation]
#tr.en: @fsux{Sa-gida}. 
#etcsl: line-id=D.24

@end trailer

@end sa-gida

@div ŋišgiŋal E

E.25. [...] {[d]}li#-pi₂-it-eš₄-tar₂ dumu {d}en-lil₂-la₂-ra
#lem: X; Lipiteštar[1]RN; dumu[child]; Enlil[1]DN
#tr.en: ……, make …… hostile to him bow down for @wRN{Lipit-@wDN{Eštar}}, the son of @wDN{Enlil}! 
#etcsl: line-id=E.25

E.26. [... erim₂-ŋal₂]-la-ni gam-gam-mu-na-ab
#lem: X; erimŋal[wicked]; gurum[bend]
#etcsl: line-id=E.26

@div trailer 

E.27. [ŋiš-gi₄-ŋal₂ sa-gid₂-da]-bi-im
#lem: ŋešgiŋal[musical refrain]; sagida[musical notation]
#tr.en: @fsux{Ŋišgiŋal} of the @fsux{sa-gida}. 
#etcsl: line-id=E.27

@end trailer

@end ŋišgiŋal

@div sa-ŋara F

F.28. [...] X a-ab-ba-ta
#lem: X; X; aʾabak[sea]
#tr.en: You have counted …… as ruin-mounds, to be mixed with dust. 
#etcsl: line-id=F.28

F.29. [...] an ki-še₃ pa e₃-ŋu₁₀-uš
#lem: X; an[sky]; ki[place]; pa[branch]; e[leave]
#tr.en: You have swept over ……, you obliterated it. 
#etcsl: line-id=F.29

F.30. [...] saŋ-zu um-mi-us₂
#lem: X; saŋ[head]; us[accompany]
#tr.en: @wDN{Ninurta}, hero of @wDN{Enlil}, 
#etcsl: line-id=F.30

F.31. [...] mu-ni-in-šid sahar-da im-da-hi
#lem: X; šid[count]; sahar[soil]; hi[mix (up)]
#tr.en: as you are sitting on your throne-dais, may your spouse, 
#etcsl: line-id=F.31

F.32. [...]-gin₇ he₂-bi₂-in-ur₄ nu-ŋal₂-la mu-ni-in-kur₉
#lem: X; ur[gather]; ŋal[⟦be⟧ to be (there]; kur[enter]
#tr.en: the true lady @wDN{Ninnibru}, who embraces you, 
#etcsl: line-id=F.32

F.33. {d}nin-urta ur-saŋ {d}en-lil₂-la₂ barag-za dur₂ ŋar-bi
#lem: Ninurtak[1]DN; ursaŋ[warrior]; Enlil[1]DN; barag[sanctum]; dur[buttocks]; ŋar[put]
#tr.en: step before you daily with friendly words on behalf of @wRN{Lipit-@wDN{Eštar}}! @wDN{Uta-ulu}, 
#etcsl: line-id=F.33

F.34. nitalam₂-zu nin zid {d}nin-nibru{ki} gu₂-da mu-ri-in#-la₂
#lem: ŋidlam[(equal ranking) spouse]; nin[lady]; zid[right]; Ninnibruk[1]DN; gu[neck]; la[hang]
#tr.en: may you be his aid when he prays! May he be able to rely on your words, 
#etcsl: line-id=F.34

F.35. inim sag₉-ga {d}li-pi₂-it-eš₄-tar₂-ra-da ud šu₂-še₃# ha-ra-da-gub
#lem: inim[word]; sag[good]; Lipiteštar[1]RN; ud[sun]; šuš[cover]; gub[stand]
#tr.en: may he be peerless! May he be the king whose fate @wDN{Ninurta} decides, 
#etcsl: line-id=F.35

F.36. u₄-ta-u₁₈-lu ki šu [il₂]-la-ni a₂-tah-ni he₂-me#-en
#lem: Utaʾulu[1]; ki[place]; šu[hand]; il[raise]; atah[helper]; me[be]
#tr.en: the one endowed with attractiveness! @wRN{Lipit-@wDN{Eštar}}, 
#etcsl: line-id=F.36

F.37. dug₄-ga-zu-ta nir he₂#-em-de₃-ŋal₂ gaba-ri-ni na-an-ŋal₂-le#
#lem: dug[speak]; nir[lordly]; ŋal[⟦be⟧ to be (there]; gabari[equal]; ŋal[⟦be⟧ to be (there]
#tr.en: the prince who is a supporter of yours, the son of @wDN{Enlil}, 
#etcsl: line-id=F.37

F.38. lugal# nam tar-ra {d}nin-urta-ke₄ ul guru₃# he₂#-en-[na-nam]
#lem: lugal[king]; nam[fate]; tar[cut]; Ninurtak[1]DN; ul[swell]; gur[lift]; me[be]
#tr.en: has established justice in @wGN{Sumer} and @wGN{Akkad}, and made the Land feel content. 
#etcsl: line-id=F.38

F.39. {[d]}li-pi₂-it-eš₄-tar₂ nun za-a-še₃ ŋal₂-la dumu {d}en-lil₂-la₂-ke₄
#lem: Lipiteštar[1]RN; nun[prince]; zaʾe[you]; ŋal[⟦be⟧ to be (there]; dumu[child]; Enlil[1]DN
#etcsl: line-id=F.39

F.40. [niŋ₂]-si-sa₂ ki-en-gi ki-uri-a mu-ni-in-ŋar
#lem: niŋsisa[justice]; Kengir[1]; Akkad[1 Akkad]; ŋar[put]
#etcsl: line-id=F.40

F.41. su kalam-ma mu-dug₃
#lem: su[flesh]; kalam[the Land (of Sumer)]; dug[good]
#etcsl: line-id=F.41

F.42. sipad mas-su₂ tum₂-tum₂-mu gal-an-zu-a uŋ₃ ha-ra-ab-lah₄-lah₄-e
#lem: sipad[shepherd]; massu[leader]; tum[bring]; galanzu[wise]; uŋ[people]; lah[plural stem of tum ⟦bring⟧]
#tr.en: May the shepherd, the expert, most wise in leading, guide the people for you! 
#etcsl: line-id=F.42

@div trailer 

F.43. sa-ŋar-ra-am₃
#lem: saŋara[musical notation]
#tr.en: @fsux{Sa-ŋara}. 
#etcsl: line-id=F.43

@end trailer

@end sa-ŋara

@div ŋišgiŋal G

G.44. ur-saŋ gal nun# {d}li-<pi₂>-it-eš₄-tar₂-ra u₃-mu-ta-sig₁₀ ki-bal nu-še-ga-na zar-gin₇ he₂-us₂-u₃-us₂
#lem: ursaŋ[warrior]; gal[big]; nun[prince]; Lipiteštar[1]RN; sig[put into]; kibala[rebel land]; šeg[agree]; zar[sheaf (of barley)]; us[accompany]
#tr.en: Great hero, when for prince @wRN{Lipit-@wDN{Eštar}} you reduce to heaps the rebellious lands which are insubordinate to him, may ……! 
#etcsl: line-id=G.44

@div trailer 

G.45. ŋiš-gi₄-ŋal₂ sa-ŋar-ra-bi-im
#lem: ŋešgiŋal[musical refrain]; saŋara[musical notation]
#tr.en: @fsux{Ŋišgiŋal} of the @fsux{sa-ŋara}. 
#etcsl: line-id=G.45

@end trailer

@end ŋišgiŋal

@div uru H

H.46. en a-ma-ru mah suhuš erim₂-ma bur₁₂-re
#lem: en[lord]; amaru[flood]; mah[great]; suhuš[foundation]; erim[enemy]; bur[tear out]
#tr.en: Lord, mighty flood which tears out the roots of the enemy! @wDN{Ninurta}, mighty flood which tears out the roots of the enemy, may you put a weapon into the mighty hands of prince @wRN{Lipit-@wDN{Eštar}} which will snap his enemies in two as if they were reeds! 
#etcsl: line-id=H.46

H.47. {d}nin-urta en a-ma-ru mah suhuš erim₂-<ma> bur₁₂-re
#lem: Ninurtak[1]DN; en[lord]; amaru[flood]; mah[great]; suhuš[foundation]; erim[enemy]; bur[tear out]
#etcsl: line-id=H.47

H.48. nun {d}li-pi₂-it-eš₄-tar₂-ra {ŋiš}tukul hul-du-ni
#lem: nun[prince]; Lipiteštar[1]RN; tukul[weapon]; huludu[wicked]
#etcsl: line-id=H.48

H.49. gi-gin₇# ša₅-ša₅ šu mah-a-ni si-bi₂-ib₂#
#lem: gi[reed]; ša[snap off]; šu[hand]; mah[great]; si[fill]
#etcsl: line-id=H.49

@div trailer 

H.50. u₁₉-ru₁₂-bi-im
#lem: uru[literary subscript]
#tr.en: Its @fsux{uru}. 
#etcsl: line-id=H.50

@end trailer

@end uru

@div trailer 

H.51. a-da-ab {d}nin-urta-ka-kam
#lem: adab[drum]; Ninurtak[1]DN
#tr.en: An @fsux{adab} of @wDN{Ninurta}. 
#etcsl: line-id=H.51

@end trailer







